    "foot_ground": "Four sensor substeps per control tick (5 ms each). For each foot contact is upward normal force >= listed Newton threshold. For the 4..15 s window count full stances/swings. A qualified touchdown follows at least 40 ms unloaded and peak sole clearance >= 5 mm. Also report threshold/80ms-10mm sensitivities. Simultaneous footfalls break ordering. Contact slip is vertically load-weighted horizontal material-point speed integrated over complete stance.",
    "historical_comparison": "The old 34000 seven-scenario data used the older effective configuration. Its later frozen-checkpoint diagnostic used the current foot-reward and material source on the same seed. Compared with latest 49999 on same scenarios, seed and explicit overrides. Runs differ in training duration and several reward/material changes. Matched within-checkpoint gait comparison uses latest +0.30 forward versus -0.40 backward. Previous direct seven and foot baselines do not share equal actual speed with latest.",
